You said "Before you *think* of doing medusa you'll now know what
tools you need", which means to me that you're saying these tools are
ones that you shouldn't attempt doing Medusa without.  Certainly
they're for the most part useful items, but they're not things that
should stop you from doing Medusa (indeed, the opposite is true for
the sack in particular).

> > Reflection's the most common way for me to deal with her.
>
> > By medusa I've almost usually ditched any pickaxe I had, if I even
> > bothered--they're useful in the mines, but after that not really worth
> > the weight to me.  Especially once I've gotten a few /digging and /
> > striking.
>
> > key/unihorn/bag are all useful but not really Medusa-related--and if
> > you haven't found a sack of any kind, that's another reason to go
> > ahead and do Medusa rather than delay it (for the sack found in
> > Perseus' statue).
>
> You've never found chests on the way down? Besides it doesn't hurt to
> exercise dex and that's the easiest way to do it.

Yes, I have.  Chests are easy enough to #force once you have an
uncursed dagger/knife or two, and even if they weren't you can leave
them until you find a key or whatever.  It _is_ extremely helpful in a
lot of cases (e.g. not waking the monsters in the Sokoban zoo, in
addition to opening chests, shops that are closed for inventory, etc),
but as far as Medusa goes you can just kick in the door (or dive past
and come up from below).

Excercising dex is incredibly minor since it's going to go up at
pretty much every opportunity anyway from throwing darts/daggers/etc,
and even if it doesn't it's hardly a make-or-break stat.

> You can't tell be that
> having an uncursed unicorn on your person at all times isn't necessary.

It's a great tool, but I've certainly (during the tournament last
month) wound up in Gehennom before finding even one.*  It sucks not
having one, but it's not related to tackling Medusa and I wouldn't
delay Medusa just for lack of a unicorn horn.

> How do *you* stop your potions and scrolls from being destroyed?

Stash them or bag them.  Failing that, having reflection and searching
until I can find a sack helps some.  That sucks, though, so finding a
sack is pretty high priority--meaning that I'm _more_ likely to
attempt Medusa a bit earlier if I don't have a sack.  Definitely not
on the "before you *think* of doing Medusa" list, rather the opposite--
if you haven't found one you may want to strongly consider tackling
medusa as there's a 50% chance of finding a sack there.

At least 2-3 times Medusa's been the first time I find any sack/bag
other than the (useless for storage purposes) bag of tricks.

* I actually had briefly poly'd a pet into a coaligned unicorn much,
much earlier--if I'd known that it would be that long until a unicorn
spawned in the game, I would have left him in the form and hoped for
his death rather than re-polying him.  In the future I may do that any
time I get a pet poly'd into a unicorn before I have a horn.  OTOH,
while not having a unicorn horn was slightly inconvenient, it didn't
really change things all _that_ much (once you have poison resistance,
it's inconvenient but not game-breakingly hard to deal without it--
certainly it's less "necessary" to me than magic resistance, poison
resistance, sleep resistance, reflection, or many other things).



